From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 03:47:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] ps5: an edition's title opens its own desktop at a cold
 start

An edition of the title (PS5-ARTCRAFT's ArtCraft) is a library entry with a
prefix of its own whose desktop the title should open by itself, the way a
PC boots into its desktop. The title reads <title folder>/edition.json once
(proton_edition): profile names that entry; hide_mihawk_desktop drops Mihawk
OS's own desktop from the library once the edition's entry is installed;
browser_shortcut is for the desktop shortcuts (next patch). Without the file
nothing changes.

A cold start (no launch request: proton_launch().requested is false) opens
the profile at once. A start that returns from a session always carries
cycle=, so a session that fails or is logged off shows the library and never
restarts itself; nor does a test run, a self-test, or a start after a
session that did not end normally (its note shows in the library). The
guided setup's first session prepares the edition's desktop instead of
Mihawk OS's.

A library entry whose executable is the desktop session's entry
(C:\windows\system32\mihawk.exe) is no longer refused as "the executable is
not there": the title starts Explorer for it, no such file exists, and a new
edition prefix has no files before its first session.

Proven: proton_launch.cpp compiles in the host-reference configuration
(g++ 13, -fsyntax-only); the ps5proton.cpp additions compile against the real
proton_launch.h in a mock of the class (its UI headers come from a sibling
repository not in this checkout). No console run: the gate battery has not
seen this commit.

